To do
=====

<sys>
-----

Replace macros in arch/mem.h with machine-defined functions that return each
required addresses. The required addresses, as of now, should be for locating
UART and the allocatable physical memory.

OpenSBI apparently jumps to the base address with one random "Boot HART". There
exists ecalls to start harts, but the number of harts has to be hard-coded as of
now. A devicetree parser may be needed. Related to the previous paragraph, the
devicetree parser is necessary for physical memory mapping.

In devicetree.c, make the devicetreeproperty search by path, and not names. Also
find out how to find memory addresses reserved to specific devices.
